.TH LIKEOS-EFIBOOT 1 "November 2026" "LikeOS" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
likeos-efiboot \- show and edit the firmware's boot entries
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B likeos-efiboot
.RB [ \-\-list ]
.RB [ \-v ]
.br
.B likeos-efiboot \-\-create \-\-disk
.I dev
.B \-\-part
.I n
.B \-\-loader
.I path
.B \-\-label
.I text
.RB [ \-\-first ]
.RB [ \-\-options
.IR text ]
.br
.B likeos-efiboot \-\-delete
.I num
.br
.B likeos-efiboot
.BI \-\-active " num"
|
.BI \-\-inactive " num"
.br
.B likeos-efiboot \-\-bootorder
.IR num , num ,...
.RB [ \-\-force ]
.br
.B likeos-efiboot
.BI \-\-bootnext " num"
|
.B \-\-delete\-bootnext
.br
.B likeos-efiboot
.BI \-\-timeout " seconds"
|
.B \-\-delete\-timeout
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B likeos-efiboot
shows and changes the boot entries of a computer's UEFI firmware: the list
the firmware's boot menu offers, and the order in which it tries them when
nobody chooses.
.PP
The firmware keeps these settings in UEFI variables of the EFI global
variable GUID:
.B Boot####
(one load option per entry: whether it is active, its label, the device
path of the loader it starts, and optional data passed to the loader),
.B BootOrder
(the entries in the order they are tried),
.B BootNext
(one entry to try on the next start only),
.B BootCurrent
(the entry the running system was started from) and
.B Timeout
(how many seconds the firmware's own menu waits).
The kernel shows every variable as a file in
.BR /sys/firmware/efi/efivars ;
on a computer started without UEFI, or with
.B efi=noruntime
on the kernel command line, the directory does not exist and
.B likeos-efiboot
says so (exit status 2).
.PP
Without an action, or with
.BR \-\-list ,
the entries are shown: BootCurrent, BootNext, the timeout and the boot
order, then one line per entry with its number, an asterisk when it is
active, its label and the device path of the loader it starts.
With
.B \-v
each entry's attributes and optional data are shown too.
.PP
Several actions may be given at once; they run in the order create, delete,
active/inactive, bootorder, bootnext, timeout.
Changing the variables needs root.
.SH ACTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-list
Show the boot entries (the default).
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-create
Create a boot entry for a loader on an EFI system partition, as a freshly
installed system needs one:
the device path
.BI HD( n ,GPT, guid , start , size )/File( loader )
is taken from the partition table of the disk given with
.BR \-\-disk ,
and the entry gets the label given with
.BR \-\-label .
An entry that already starts the same loader from the same partition is
reused rather than duplicated (and given the new label and options).
Needs
.BR \-\-disk ,
.BR \-\-part ,
.B \-\-loader
and
.BR \-\-label .
.TP
.BR \-B ", " \-\-delete " \fInum\fR"
Delete entry
.I num
and take it out of the boot order.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-active " \fInum\fR"
Mark entry
.I num
active: the firmware tries it.
.TP
.BR \-A ", " \-\-inactive " \fInum\fR"
Mark entry
.I num
inactive: it stays in the list but the firmware passes over it.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-bootorder " \fInum\fR,\fInum\fR,..."
Set the boot order.
Numbers of entries that do not exist are refused unless
.B \-\-force
is given.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-bootnext " \fInum\fR"
Start entry
.I num
on the next start only; the firmware deletes BootNext when it uses it.
.TP
.BR \-N ", " \-\-delete\-bootnext
Cancel BootNext.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-timeout " \fIseconds\fR"
Set how long the firmware's own boot menu waits.
.TP
.BR \-T ", " \-\-delete\-timeout
Remove the timeout setting (the firmware's default applies).
.SH CREATE OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-disk " \fIdev\fR"
The disk that holds the EFI system partition
.RB ( /dev/sda ,
.BR /dev/nvme0n1 ).
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-part " \fIn\fR"
The number of the EFI system partition on it.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-loader " \fIpath\fR"
The loader's path on that partition, with backslashes:
.BR \eEFI\eLIKEOS\eBOOTX64.EFI .
.TP
.BR \-L ", " \-\-label " \fItext\fR"
The name the firmware's boot menu shows.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-first
Put the entry first in the boot order (otherwise it is added at the end).
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-options " \fItext\fR"
Optional data passed to the loader (as UCS-2 text).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-force
Accept entry numbers in
.B \-\-bootorder
that have no entry.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Report errors only.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Show the attributes and optional data of the entries too.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a summary of the actions and options.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version.
.PP
.I num
is a hexadecimal entry number:
.BR 3 ,
.B 0003
and
.B Boot0003
are the same entry.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The action failed.
.TP
.B 2
Wrong usage, or the system has no UEFI variables.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LIKEOS_EFIVARS_DIR
A directory used in place of
.B /sys/firmware/efi/efivars
(for tests).
.SH FILES
.TP
.BI /sys/firmware/efi/efivars/ Name \- GUID
One UEFI variable: four bytes of attributes (little-endian) followed by
its value.
Writing the file in one
.BR write (2)
sets the variable,
.BR unlink (2)
deletes it.
.SH EXAMPLES
The entry the installer creates for a LikeOS installation whose EFI system
partition is the first partition of /dev/nvme0n1:
.PP
.RS
.nf
likeos\-efiboot \-\-create \-\-disk /dev/nvme0n1 \-\-part 1 \e
        \-\-loader '\eEFI\eLIKEOS\eBOOTX64.EFI' \e
        \-\-label LikeOS \-\-first
.fi
.RE
.PP
Start entry 0004 once, on the next start:
.PP
.RS
.nf
likeos\-efiboot \-\-bootnext 4
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR likeos-install (1),
.BR likeos-gpt (1)
